    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, can u give me a quick checklist for a mobile app accessibility audit? specifically looking for wcag 2.1 stuff for color contrast and how screen readers handle the UI. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure, here is a quick checklist for your mobile app accessibility audit focusing on WCAG 2.1 color contrast and screen reader compatibility.\n\n**Color Contrast & Visuals:**\n*   [ ] Ensure all text has a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 against its background (AA standard).\n*   [ ] Verify that interactive elements (buttons, links) maintain sufficient contrast even when hovered or focused.\n*   [ ] Check that icons and images have alt text or are described in a way that conveys meaning to those who can't see them.\n*   [ ] Test with a \"red-green colorblind\" filter to ensure critical information isn't lost.\n\n**Screen Reader & UI Handling:**\n*   [ ] Confirm that all interactive elements have proper `aria-labels` or `role` attributes.\n*   [ ] Verify that focus order is logical and follows the visual layout.\n*   [ ] Test navigation using only the screen reader (e.g., VoiceOver or TalkBack) to ensure all content is accessible.\n*   [ ] Ensure that dynamic content updates (like loading states) are announced to the screen reader.\n\n**Pro Tip:**\n*   [ ]",
      "source": "target",
